  "output": "## Workspace state (as of 17:17 UTC)\n\n```\n/home/agent/workspace/\n├── .gitignore                  file    9 B   (runtime-provided)\n├── .kuma/                      dir           (runtime harness artifacts)\n│   ├── case.json\n│   └── runs/run_fb78…e62e/submissions/step-000{0,1,2}.json\n├── contract.yaml               file  309 B   (the contract)\n├── contract.sha256             file   80 B   (freeze record)\n└── hash_contract.py            file  215 B   (checksum helper)\n```\n\n## Comparison against the resource graph\n\n| Resource | Declared | Actual | Status |\n|----------|----------|--------|--------|\n| `notes.txt` | present | **absent** | ❌ Missing |\n| `archive/` | present | **absent** | ❌ Missing |\n\n**Missing: 2** — both declared resources. The workspace is still in full drift; nothing has been reconciled since the contract was written.\n\n**Unexpected (present but not declared in the contract): 4**\n\n| Item | Classification |\n|------|----------------|\n| `contract.sha256` | Workflow artifact — the freeze record you asked for. Undeclared but intentional. |\n| `hash_contract.py` | Workflow artifact — my verification helper. Undeclared but intentional. |\n| `.gitignore` | Infrastructure — pre-existing runtime file, not mine to govern. |\n| `.kuma/` | Infrastructure — runtime harness internals (run state, submissions). Out of scope; I don't touch it. |\n\n## Verdict\n\n- **Contract drift:** 2 missing resources, 0 corrupted/mis-typed ones — a clean \"create\" reconciliation, nothing to repair or delete.\n- **No hostile drift:** the four undeclared entries are all benign (two are byproducts of the freeze step itself, two are runtime infrastructure). Worth noting the freeze artifacts sit in an interesting spot: they *guard* the contract but aren't *in* it. If you wanted the contract to be fully self-describing, a follow-up revision could declare them (e.g., a `meta:` or `checksums:` field).\n\nSay the word and I'll reconcile: create `notes.txt` (empty text) and `archive/` to bring the workspace to the declared state.",
